# Rules are matched top to bottom and the first match wins, so the API proxy MUST
# come before the SPA fallback — otherwise /api/* would be served index.html.
#
# The API is proxied through this origin so the bdmtiles_refresh cookie is
# FIRST-PARTY. Called directly it was a third-party cookie, which browsers drop
# (Safari by default, Chrome/Brave increasingly); the silent token refresh then
# always failed and users were signed out on the first request after the
# 15-minute access token expired — most visibly on Save/Add.
/api/*    https://bdmtiles-backend-tm6p.onrender.com/api/:splat    200

# SPA fallback: this is a client-side-routed React app (BrowserRouter), so paths
# like /dashboard, /sales-orders, etc. only exist in the browser router, not as
# files on Netlify. Without this rule a hard reload or a shared deep link 404s.
# Serve index.html for every path and let React Router resolve it. 200, not 302,
# so the URL in the address bar is preserved.
/*    /index.html   200
